# No frontend environment variables are required.
#
# Build-time only (read by vite.config.ts, never shipped to the browser):
#   MUTABA3A_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://<landing host>
#     The https origin where the landing is served. The web build puts it in
#     the link-preview tags (og:url, og:image) and the /hosted canonical; the
#     hosted build puts it in the portal sign-in's "No account? Request one"
#     link (MUT-188). Defaults to the landing origin config/hosts.json names
#     (MUT-326; `npm run --silent hosts -- get landingOrigin`); set it only for
#     a staging host. An origin the config doesn't name must also be added to
#     BOTH lists in scripts/bundle-origins.json.
#   MUTABA3A_PORTAL_URL=https://<portal host>
#     The hosted portal's https origin, opened by the landing's sign-in and
#     signup links (MUT-187, MUT-369). Defaults to the portal origin
#     config/hosts.json names; a bad value fails the build. An origin the
#     config doesn't name must also be added to scripts/bundle-origins.json.
#
# Release-only telemetry (ADR-236; the same rule in every Barmajiyat app).
# Sentry and PostHog send only from a production build (`vite build` outside
# Netlify or in Netlify's production context) served on the production host
# config/hosts.json names: the apex for the website, app.<apex> for the
# portal. Never the dev server, deploy previews, the legacy Netlify and Cloud
# Run hosts, localhost previews, tests or release-QA. One override each,
# read when the build runs (src/lib/telemetry/telemetryGate.ts):
#   SENTRY_ENABLED=false     unset = the rule above; false = off even in a
#   POSTHOG_ENABLED=false    production build (local release builds, QA, e2e);
#                            true = on anywhere, only to check the integration
# `npm run dev*` and the release-QA config default both to false. A missing key
# or DSN is always off. Every event is tagged with its environment (Sentry
# `environment`, PostHog `environment`: production | development).
#
# Error reporting (ADR-091, MUT-146; wired by MUT-149 portal and MUT-150 landing).
# Values come from `terraform output -json dsn` in server/infrastructure/sentry.
#   MUTABA3A_LANDING_SENTRY_DSN=https://<public key>@<id>.ingest.de.sentry.io/<project>   Netlify, production context
#   MUTABA3A_SENTRY_DSN=https://<public key>@<id>.ingest.de.sentry.io/<project>           deploy.env, the portal build
# Usage analytics (ADR-090): the PostHog project key, both builds.
#   MUTABA3A_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_...
# Build-time only, for the source-map upload; NEVER prefix these with VITE_
# (Vite inlines every VITE_ variable into the browser bundle):
#   SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=sntrys_...      upload-only org token; Netlify build env / operator shell
#   SENTRY_ORG=mutaba3a
#   SENTRY_PROJECT=mutaba3a-landing   (or mutaba3a-portal for the hosted build)
